---
const steps = [
  [
    "Benchmark",
    "Establish the baseline.",
    "Model, hardware, workload, concurrency, latency, throughput, and GPU utilization. Same conditions. Useful comparisons.",
  ],
  [
    "Profile",
    "Find the time. Follow the memory.",
    "Read the timeline. Separate compute, bandwidth, communication, and waiting. Locate the constraint before touching the code.",
  ],
  [
    "Optimize",
    "Attack the highest-value bottleneck.",
    "Configuration, scheduling, memory, or a specialized kernel. Pick the intervention the measurements actually support.",
  ],
  [
    "Validate",
    "Make the result survive reality.",
    "Check correctness and measure again under realistic load. Document tradeoffs, regressions, and a reproducible benchmark.",
  ],
];
---

<section class="section container" id="process">
  <div class="section-heading reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">06 / HOW THE WORK HAPPENS</p>
    <h2>
      No optimization
      <br />
      <span class="text-accent">without measurement.</span>
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="process-grid">
    {steps.map(([title, line, text], i) => (
      <article class="process-step reveal">
        <span class="step-number mono">
          0{i + 1}
          <span>↗</span>
        </span>
        <h3>{title}</h3>
        <strong>{line}</strong>
        <p>{text}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="process-note mono reveal">
    <span>↳</span> NO VICTORY SCREENSHOTS FROM UNREALISTIC MICROBENCHMARKS.
  </p>
</section>
